Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:58:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kiln: Reboot and Shutdown rows each ask for their own action

Advanced's Power section lists Reboot and Shutdown as two rows, but both
opened the same dialog, which offers Reboot and Shutdown again: tapping
Reboot still asked which of the two.

On HELIX_KILN_AD5X builds (helix::kiln_host_power()) each row now asks
only for its own action (show_power_entry_dialog): Reboot asks "Restart
the printer?" with Restart and Cancel, Shutdown asks "Shut down the
printer?" with Shutdown (styled as danger) and Cancel. A confirmation
goes through Moonraker's machine.reboot or machine.shutdown as before
(request_kiln_power, which request_kiln_reboot now calls): Kiln's update
agent decides, a refusal is a toast with its reason, without a connection
"Not connected to the printer", and nothing is powered off locally. An
accepted request shows "Restarting printer..." or "Shutting down
printer...". The rows stay greyed while a job holds the machine
(kiln_power_locked).

The home screen's power tile keeps the dialog with both actions: it is the
one power entry there (the widget is "Shutdown/Reboot", "Shut down or
restart the host").

Other builds keep upstream's dialog behind both rows. Strings in en and
ru.

Tests: the questions' texts; on Kiln the real Advanced panel's Reboot row
asks only to restart and sends machine.reboot on Restart, nothing on
Cancel, the refusal toast with its reason; the Shutdown row the same for
machine.shutdown; nothing sent without a connection; other builds open
upstream's dialog from both rows.

Settings > Safety & Alerts: HelixScreen 1.2's "Confirm shutdown and
reboot" switch (row_power_confirm) sets whether upstream's power dialog
asks first. On Kiln the Reboot and Shutdown rows always ask, so the
switch would do nothing: SafetySettingsOverlay::on_activate() hides the
row when helix::kiln_host_power() is true. Other builds keep it. Test:
the row hidden on Kiln, shown elsewhere.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
